{
  "_meta": {
    "source": "memo.ac / MemoAI v1.7.5 (macOS arm64) — Resources/presets/whisper-models.js + Resources/plugins/extra-transcription-plugins.json",
    "extractedBy": "memo-compare (T-113)",
    "extractedAt": "2026-08-03",
    "purpose": "Factual interoperability reference for aligning OpenMemo's ASR model picker. Data catalog only (ids, sizes, grouping axes) — not memo.ac source code.",
    "scopeNote": "ADR-016 decided OpenMemo ships whisper only. sherpa/parakeet/funasr are recorded here for completeness and marked outOfScope=true. The VALUABLE part for us is `uiPresentation` below, not the extra engines.",
    "totals": {
      "asrModelEntries": 47,
      "whisper": 15,
      "sherpaAsr": 27,
      "parakeet": 4,
      "funasr": 1
    },
    "criticalObservation": "All 15 whisper entries are f16. memo.ac offers NO quantization choice. OpenMemo's 25 whisper entries include quant tiers, so our list is LONGER than theirs and needs the grouping below even more."
  },
  "uiPresentation": {
    "_note": "THIS is the part worth copying — how 15 entries avoid looking like a wall.",
    "surfaceA_transcriptionQuickPicker": {
      "component": "renderer fn `Far` (+ `kJe` index builder)",
      "mechanism": "TWO-AXIS FILTER, not a flat list",
      "axis1": {
        "field": "lang",
        "control": "Select",
        "values": [
          "multi",
          "en",
          "zh",
          "ja"
        ]
      },
      "axis2": {
        "field": "speedValue",
        "control": "Tabs",
        "values": [
          "fast",
          "balance",
          "quality"
        ]
      },
      "renderedSet": "models.filter(m => m.lang === selectedLang && m.speedValue === selectedSpeed)",
      "resultingCardCount": "typically 1-3 of 15 visible at once",
      "cardStyle": "fixed-size tiles (w-40 h-28, border-2), NOT dropdown rows",
      "perTierHintKeys": [
        "model.fast mode hint",
        "model.balanced mode hint",
        "model.quality mode hint"
      ],
      "statusLine": "shows `model.current model` + label, else `model.download models`",
      "indexBuilder": "kJe(models) -> {modes: lang->langLabel, speeds: speedValue->speedLabel, sortModels: lang->models[]} — grouping index derived FROM the model list, no hardcoded groups"
    },
    "surfaceB_modelManagementList": {
      "location": "Settings -> model management",
      "mechanism": "language Select (default option `model.all models`) + section-per-language when 'all'",
      "rowContent": "label + '(not downloaded)' muted tag + checkmark on the active one",
      "sectionHeader": "small muted language label per group"
    },
    "surfaceC_extraEngineList": {
      "displayNameCleanup": "strips the `sherpa-onnx-streaming-` prefix before display",
      "rowContent": "cleaned name + size in parens + '(not downloaded)' tag + active checkmark"
    },
    "recommendationForOpenMemo": [
      "Our 25 whisper entries are MORE than their 15 -> a flat dropdown is strictly worse for us than for them.",
      "Adopt the two-axis filter (language x speed/quality tier). We already have `quantTier` (small/balanced/quality) and `languages` on every manifest entry, so both axes exist in our data with no schema change.",
      "Our extra axis (quantization) should be a THIRD level: pick model group first, then quant variant — we already group by `groupId`, so render groupId as the card and quant as a segmented control inside the detail.",
      "Keep the per-tier hint text: a tier is meaningless without a one-line explanation of the tradeoff.",
      "Show download state inline on the row/card rather than in a separate 'installed' tab."
    ]
  },
